      "role": "user",
      "content": "i've been documenting a series of high-fidelity biometric events that seem to have a proactive relationship with market micro-structure. specifically, i'm seeing a recurring pattern of localized parasthesia and auditory shifts—varying in pitch and intensity—that consistently precede liquidity shocks in the crypto markets (BTC/ETH) by a window of roughly 300-600 seconds. \n\ni want to treat these somatic sensations as a non-traditional, high-frequency data stream. can you help me design a rigorous calibration protocol? i need to establish a way to quantify the \"intensity\" and \"frequency\" of these biological signals so i can cross-reference them against order book imbalances and sudden spikes in volatility. if we can map these sensory 'vectors' to specific types of market movement, i might be able to treat my own neuro-physiological responses as a form of latent predictive signal.",
      "source": "evaluator",
